ATTRIBUTION

    Khaliq, A. A. (2026). Operator-annotated EUR-Lex corpus for defeasible
    legal text classification. Released with the doctoral thesis "When Does
    Structure Help? Disentangling Mechanism from Capacity in
    Defeasibility-Aware Legal Text Classification", University of Milan.
    https://github.com/oziofficial5/jusdefv2

SCOPE AND PROVENANCE

The operator labels are released as label files keyed to the public dataset
identifiers of the source corpora. Source text is not redistributed here.

  - EUR-Lex source text is reusable under the European Commission's reuse
    policy with attribution to the source.
  - LEDGAR and ECtHR are used under their respective LexGLUE and
    AUEB-NLP terms and are not redistributed.
  - CUAD is used under the terms of the Atticus Project release and is not
    redistributed.

Obtain the underlying corpora from their original providers.

KNOWN LIMITATION

Candidate labels were generated automatically and validated by human
annotation at Cohen's kappa = 0.77 against an independent annotator (N = 300).
Reliability against expert legal judgement is bounded by that figure. The
accompanying neural detector has per-class recall of 0.771 on NEG, with the
dominant error being NEG misread as OVR. Neither resource should be placed on
a path where an unreviewed operator label reaches a user or an automated
decision.
